docs/development.md:491:Reminders pending/returned/history destinations (also G then H and palette).
DESIGN.md:254:   - **Reminders (phase 2).** A list context (`'reminders'`, fixture only, `remindersSupported`) beside Done and Trash, entered from the header glyph (`Reminders (G then H)`, `aria-current="page"` and Paper White while the list is showing), `G H`, the palette and the navigator, and from `H` (`Remind me`) on an Inbox row or an open reader. There is no new rail slot and no new backend call: the rows are `client.reminders.list()` plus the live change subscription, read through `useReminders` (which holds every request rule of the old drawer: per-request staleness, exact retry of a lost ACK, the validation message for `dueAt`, the newer-message preparation error). The context is pushed on the history stack, so Back and Escape return to the prior context and row, and a reader opened from a reminder returns to the same reminder row (J/K do not walk between reminders).
DESIGN.md:397:- **Style:** a Lifted Charcoal panel, 10px radius, 576px max width, no border, Overlay lift, 15vh from the top. There is no caption: the placeholder and the dialog's accessible name say whether it is Commands or Destinations. The 38px query (16px Headline) sits on Deep Umber with a 1px Dusk Lavender border; it always owns keyboard focus, so that border is its focus indicator. Items are 36px rows of 12px Body with a 16px Graphite glyph that turns Paper White when highlighted. The highlighted item gets a Focus Stone fill plus a 3px Dusk Lavender left bar. Disabled items are Smoke, with their reason in Ash. Shortcuts are `kbd` in Ash on Deep Umber, compact ("G then E", timing in the tooltip). The hint line sits under a 1px Seam.
